<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sobek</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sobek was the ancient Egyptian crocodile god, associated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>, fertility and the power of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a>. His main cult centres were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shedet">Shedet</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faiyum">Faiyum</a> and Kom Ombo in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a>. The kings of the Twelfth and Thirteenth Dynasties honoured him especially, and several, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sobekneferu">Sobekneferu</a> and the Sobekhoteps, bore his name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sobek.jpg" alt="Sobek" width="320" height="768" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeff Dahl · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sobek.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
